sdata> -- Issue #71 / systems-designer Finding 2: REMOVE n[-m]'s line-editor
sdata> -- parser used to call Real'Value unconditionally on the token following
sdata> -- '-', assuming it was always Token_Numeric_Literal. A .i/.n literal
sdata> -- (Token_Infinity/Token_NaN) carries no text, so this used to raise an
sdata> -- uncaught Constraint_Error ("Internal error"-shaped) instead of a clean,
sdata> -- descriptive error. Confirms both the bare-argument and range-argument
sdata> -- positions are guarded, and that the REPL keeps accepting input after
sdata> -- the error (same recovery contract as repl_error_recovery.cmd).
sdata> LET A = 1
sdata> LET A = 2
sdata> LET A = 3
sdata> REMOVE .i
Error: REMOVE requires a program-buffer line number; Infinity/NaN literals (.i, .n) are not valid here
sdata> REMOVE 1-.n
Error: REMOVE requires a program-buffer line number; Infinity/NaN literals (.i, .n) are not valid here
sdata> RUN
RUN complete. 1 records and 1 variables processed.
sdata> PRINT A
sdata> RUN
3.00000
RUN complete. 1 records and 1 variables processed.
sdata> QUIT
